<h2>Use the playbooks with an AI assistant</h2>
<p>Each playbook has an agent skill. A skill for a playbook of plays teaches an assistant to match a situation to a play, check when not to use it, and say plainly whether a real instance of the play is recorded. A skill for a framework teaches it to read a situation through the framework. Add a skill in Claude under Settings, then Capabilities, then Skills. Agents can also find them at <a href="/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json">/.well-known/agent-skills/</a>.</p>
<p>Every playbook and play is available as <a href="/playbooks.json">JSON</a>, and each page has a Markdown version at the same address ending in <code>.md</code>, such as <a href="/playbooks/okrs/two-functions.md">/playbooks/okrs/two-functions.md</a>.</p>
